==Battleground==
*1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*1 [[Project A]] spawns after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*2 [[Cyberhorn]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Project A]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Project A]] spawns after 140 seconds<sup>4,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]] and [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]] can take advantage of the slow-moving Cyberhorns to slowly damage the THE SLOTH and Project A. [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Major Leaguer Cat]] is also quite useful given its Long Distance and Resistance to [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]].

With enough [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] can carry the stage, with assistance from high-damage units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]. Assuming you have enough [[Treasure]]s, a high-leveled [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can also solo the stage with its exceptional damage and [[Immune to Warp]] Ability. Project A will either die or be knocked back behind the base, and as long as your units don't get pushed back by THE SLOTH, the base will be destroyed. The base can even be killed before THE SLOTH and Cyberhorns spawn with enough damage output.

This stage becomes an absolute joke with all Anti-Starred Alien Treasures, as you can kill the first Project A with just Maglev, then send in other attackers to destroy the enemy base early.

